    <!-- ============================================================
         OVERVIEW
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section-tight cs-overview">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header reveal text-center">
                <span class="eyebrow" style="justify-content: center;">overview</span>
                <h2>What is <br><span class="grad-text">C# Mastery Hub?</span></h2>
                <p class="cs-section-lead">
                    A structured, free learning platform that takes beginners from installing Visual Studio all the way to building full-stack ASP.NET Core apps, deploying to Azure and AWS, and using DevOps practices — all in plain English, with no registration required.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="cs-overview-grid">
                <div class="cs-overview-card reveal" style="--stagger-index:0">
                    <span class="cs-overview-kicker">01 — Mission</span>
                    <h3>Free, complete C# education</h3>
                    <p>Quality programming education should be accessible to everyone. This site delivers a full beginner-to-professional curriculum with no paywalls, no ads, and no login wall.</p>
                    <span class="cs-overview-arrow">↗</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-overview-card reveal" style="--stagger-index:1">
                    <span class="cs-overview-kicker">02 — Architecture</span>
                    <h3>Razor Pages + service layer</h3>
                    <p>Each feature (SEO, quizzes, code challenges, discussions) is backed by a dedicated service registered in DI. Pages stay thin; logic lives in <code>Services/</code> and models in <code>Models/</code>.</p>
                    <span class="cs-overview-arrow">↗</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-overview-card reveal" style="--stagger-index:2">
                    <span class="cs-overview-kicker">03 — Experience</span>
                    <h3>Beginner → Master, in one path</h3>
                    <p>Three levels — Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced — guide learners through 19 topics, with per-lesson quizzes, interactive code challenges, and a discussion forum for each topic.</p>
                    <span class="cs-overview-arrow">↗</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

