    <!-- ============================================================
         BUILD STORY
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section-tight cs-story">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header reveal text-center">
                <span class="eyebrow" style="justify-content: center;">build-story</span>
                <h2>How it was <br><span class="grad-text">built.</span></h2>
            </div>

            <ol class="cs-timeline">
                <li class="cs-timeline-item reveal" style="--stagger-index:0">
                    <span class="cs-timeline-dot"></span>
                    <div class="cs-timeline-body">
                        <span class="cs-timeline-step">Phase 01</span>
                        <h3>Curriculum architecture</h3>
                        <p>Mapped out 19 topics across three levels — Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced — and designed a consistent page template with breadcrumbs, sidebar navigation, lesson badges, and previous/next links.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="cs-timeline-item reveal" style="--stagger-index:1">
                    <span class="cs-timeline-dot"></span>
                    <div class="cs-timeline-body">
                        <span class="cs-timeline-step">Phase 02</span>
                        <h3>Service-layer backend</h3>
                        <p>Registered <code>SeoService</code>, <code>QuizService</code>, <code>ChallengeService</code>, and <code>DiscussionService</code> in DI. Each Razor Page depends only on its service — page models stay thin and testable.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="cs-timeline-item reveal" style="--stagger-index:2">
                    <span class="cs-timeline-dot"></span>
                    <div class="cs-timeline-body">
                        <span class="cs-timeline-step">Phase 03</span>
                        <h3>Interactive learning</h3>
                        <p>Built quizzes with graded results, code challenges with starter code and solutions, and a threaded discussion forum — each tied to its lesson via shared topic IDs.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="cs-timeline-item reveal" style="--stagger-index:3">
                    <span class="cs-timeline-dot"></span>
                    <div class="cs-timeline-body">
                        <span class="cs-timeline-step">Phase 04</span>
                        <h3>SEO &amp; deployment</h3>
                        <p>Integrated <code>SeoService</code> for per-page meta tags and OpenGraph data, added security headers and HSTS, then deployed to Render with HTTPS enforced in production.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         FEATURES
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section-tight cs-features">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header reveal text-center">
                <span class="eyebrow" style="justify-content: center;">features</span>
                <h2>What makes this <br><span class="grad-text">platform stand out.</span></h2>
            </div>

            <div class="cs-features-grid">
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:0">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">📚</div>
                    <h3>19-topic curriculum</h3>
                    <p>From "Getting Started" to DevOps, AWS, and a full WinForms project walkthrough — every topic has a dedicated lesson set, breadcrumb, and prev/next navigation.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Structured</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:1">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">🧠</div>
                    <h3>Interactive quizzes</h3>
                    <p>Each lesson has a companion quiz backed by <code>QuizService</code>. Results are graded, explained, and shown with per-answer feedback.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Assessment</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:2">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">⚙️</div>
                    <h3>Code challenges</h3>
                    <p>Difficulty-filtered challenges with starter code, a reference solution, and a written explanation — backed by <code>ChallengeService</code> and modeled in <code>CodeChallenge</code>.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Practice</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:3">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">💬</div>
                    <h3>Discussion forum</h3>
                    <p>Per-topic threads with replies, pinned posts, view counts, and author names — backed by <code>DiscussionService</code>. A real community layer, not just comments.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Community</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:4">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">🔎</div>
                    <h3>Central SEO service</h3>
                    <p><code>SeoService</code> generates per-page titles, descriptions, canonical URLs, and OpenGraph metadata — so every lesson page is indexable and shareable.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Discoverable</span>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-feature reveal" style="--stagger-index:5">
                    <div class="cs-feature-icon">🛡️</div>
                    <h3>Production hardening</h3>
                    <p>HSTS, HTTPS redirect, exception handler, and user-secrets integration in development. Deployed to Render and live on the public internet.</p>
                    <span class="cs-feature-tag">Production</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

